 "answerVoice": "male",
 "notes": "Only the man in orange shorts can be followed; the other jumpers change every half second and overlap, so all three phrases use him. He falls backwards at 0-0.5 s and lies on his back 1.0-3.5 s; from 4.0 he is only a sliver at the left edge (off at 5.5, 6.5, 7.5-9.0 where only a scrap of orange shows). Other people also end up lying in the blocks later but are mostly buried. Still 2.0: 'a man' and 'shorts' are on the same (large) figure, 0.2 apart in y; a second man's body is cut off at the top right. 'blocks' could in principle label any part of the pit; its slot is on blocks only."
